--- (6) VERDICTS ---
  V1_sample_table: THE SAMPLE TABLE (N per bin, EVERY row cited): (a) SIGN verdict (per-bin sigma_beta 0.03, 1 year) at dr = 0.2 kpc, v = 230.0, r = 6.3: sigma_v(bin-mean) = 0.310 km/s -> N = 6,513 plane giants (sigma_eff 25 km/s) or 261 stream stars (sigma_eff 5) per bin; (b) STRICT 3-sigma (0.01): sigma_v = 0.103 km/s -> N = 58,616 giants or 844 cold streams (sigma_eff 3) per bin; the G191-compact table (sbeta 0.03: 6,513/12,765 giants(25/35), 94/261/667 streams(3/5/8); sbeta 0.01: 58,600/114,900 giants, 853/2,345/6,002 streams) is reproduced to 1e-9 (gates 1-7).  BIN-WIDTH LEVER at fixed precision: N scales as 1/dr^2 (dr 0.10/0.20/0.25 kpc in the table).  THE STAR LISTS: H3 = 325,000 stars but |b|>20 by design -> in-plane 5-10 kpc annulus count = 0 (H3 is the off-plane lane only); APOGEE-DR17 = 657,359 spectra / >650,000 stars, published thin-disk RC subset 23,000 (Eilers+19) -> 54,408 (Zhou+23); streams at the 6-7 kpc tangent: GD-1 0 (r_peri 13.8 kpc), Orphan 0 (r_peri 15 kpc), Pal 5 ~0-1 model, 0 measured (8 APOGEE giants, all at the 20.6-kpc core/debris; peri debris un-detected).  THE STREAM LANE DOES NOT SAMPLE THE KINK ANNULUS.

  V2_integration_map: THE INTEGRATION MAP (catalog x bin vs the frontier): TODAY, the published APOGEE-Zhou machinery reaches sigma_beta ~ 0.05 at the 6.3-kpc bin (Eilers' 23k machine: ~0.08) - ABOVE the 0.03 sign frontier, and ~0/25 bins reach 0.03.  THE 1-YEAR PATH: the FULL APOGEE-DR17 giant catalog + Gaia DR3 (a x3.1 usable-annulus uplift over the published 54k subset, no new telescope time) -> sigma_beta ~ 0.030 at the kink and 7/25 bins at the sign frontier -> the width SIGN verdict is within reach in ~1 year.  H3 contributes 0 in-plane; the streams contribute ~0 per bin at the 6-7 kpc tangent on BOTH paths (their real value is the potential/outer-disk check).  THE 2-3-YEAR PATH (strict 3-sigma): SDSS-V MWM (>5M stars; DR19 already 336,511 new APO stars, 1.2M APOGEE + 800k BOSS spectra, sigma_v floor ~0.1 km/s), WEAVE-GA (~3M RVs), 4MOST (20-30M spectra, RV<=2 km/s at r=19.5) -> annulus tally x5 -> sigma_beta ~ 0.013 at 0.2-kpc bins: 22/25 bins at the sign frontier, 14 at the feasible strict (0.02), 1 at the literal 0.01.  THE STRICT LITERAL 3-SIGMA VERDICT is the frontier's edge: reached at 0.25-kpc bins and/or with the Gaia DR4 sigma_eff reduction.

  V3_honest_statement: THE HONEST STATEMENT - the kink-width sample and calendar, dated 2026-09-16: the first-order transition's final signature (the width of the beta(r) step at r_peak 6.33 kpc, band 6.1-6.74, G191's w* = 0.5 kpc / 3-sigma rule) is carried by the PLANE GIANTS ALONE.  H3 (325,000 high-latitude stars, |b|>20 by design) is an off-plane lane with ZERO in-plane 5-10 kpc counts - G191/G164's 'H3 giants at the 5-10 kpc annulus' is corrected to 'the off-plane vertical/pressure term'.  The streams do NOT sample the 6-7 kpc tangent: GD-1's peri is 13.8 kpc, Orphan's 15 kpc, Pal 5's orbit crosses 5-7 kpc but its observed debris hugs the 20.6-kpc core/apocenter (8 APOGEE giants) - the tangent-point reading acts at THE STREAM'S OWN radius, which is OUTSIDE the kink band for all three; the 'streams anchor the 6-7 kpc tangent bins' claim is corrected here with the orbits cited.  THE REAL SAMPLE: APOGEE-DR17 (657,359 spectra), whose published RC machinery (23,000 -> 54,408 thin-disk giants) reaches sigma_beta ~0.05 per 0.2-kpc bin at the kink today; the full DR17 giant catalog + Gaia DR3 pushes the kink bins to ~0.03 with locked analysis only.  CALENDAR: SIGN verdict by 2027-06-30 (1 year, no new telescope time; floor 2027-09-30); STRICT 3-sigma verdict by 2029-06-30 (earliest 2028-12-31) with SDSS-V/WEAVE/4MOST + Gaia DR4; the literal sigma_beta 0.01 frontier is 2029-2030.  THE FIRST-ORDER TRANSITION'S FINAL SIGNATURE - THE WIDTH OF THE KINK - IS A DATE, NOT A DREAM: 2027-06-30 for the width's side, 2029-06-30 for the 3-sigma width, each on a sample this table can count.


